  "id": "399c37cc-8309-582f-a071-67bd7c7cfb14",
  "slug": "texas-cowboy-quiche-recipe-11690639",
  "name": "Texas Cowboy Quiche",
  "recipe_type": "breakfast",
  "brief_description": "This Texas cowboy quiche has a pressed-in crust and many of the flavors of a breakfast taco. It\u2019s great with cherry tomatoes, sliced tomatoes, avocado slices, pico de gallo\u2014in any combination\u2014on the side, or fresh fruit.",
  "cuisine": "Tex-Mex",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "For crust, combine flour, oats, and salt in the bowl of a food processor and pulse 2 or 3 times to mix, then process until oats and flour are uniform. Add vegetable oil, and pulse a few times to mix. Add water, 1 tablespoon at a time, pulsing a few times after each addition, until dough begins to come together into a ball."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "With fingertips, press dough into a 9-inch quiche pan or pie pan in a thin, even layer on the bottom and up the sides. Refrigerate until ready to fill."
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "text": "Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (180 degrees C)."
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "text": "For filling, Place bacon in a large nonstick skillet and cook over medium-high heat, turning occasionally, until evenly browned, about 10 minutes. Drain bacon on paper towels; pour off bacon grease and discard. Crumble bacon when cool enough to handle."
    },
    {
      "position": 5,
      "text": "Add chorizo to the skillet; cook and stir, breaking up large clumps with a spatula, until browned and crumbly, about 5 minutes. Drain; wipe out the skillet."
    },
    {
      "position": 6,
      "text": "Melt butter in the same large nonstick skillet over medium heat. When butter stops sizzling, add onions and cook, stirring occasionally, until soft and translucent, about 3 minutes."
    },
    {
      "position": 7,
      "text": "Add bell peppers; continue cooking until vegetables are very tender, stirring occasionally, about 5 minutes. Stir in hash browns; cook for about 2 minutes. Remove from heat; stir in green chilies, bacon, chorizo, and remaining 1/2 cup Cheddar cheese; set aside."
    },
    {
      "position": 8,
      "text": "Break eggs into a large bowl, and add half-and-half, sour cream, salt, black pepper, and cayenne. Whisk egg mixture until well blended, and stir in vegetable-bacon mixture."
    },
    {
      "position": 9,
      "text": "Remove crust from the refrigerator and place on a rimmed baking sheet. Pour in filling and distribute evenly across the bottom of the crust."
    },
    {
      "position": 10,
      "text": "Bake quiche in the center of the preheated oven until a knife inserted in the center comes out clean, 35 to 55 minutes. Remove quiche to a cooling rack; sprinkle remaining 1/2 cup Cheddar on top while still hot. Cool on the rack for 10 minutes. Cut into 8 servings."
    }
  ],
  "servings": 8,
  "cooking_time_minutes": 95,
  "preparation_time_minutes": 30,
